<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transitional Federal Government</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2004">2004</a>–<a href="/years/2012">2012</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Transitional Federal Government was the internationally recognised government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> from 2004 to 2012. Formed at peace talks in Kenya, with a parliament chosen by clan quotas, it struggled to control even Mogadishu and depended on Ethiopian troops and then on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a> force <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union-mission-to-somalia">AMISOM</a>. In 2012 it was replaced by the Federal Government of Somalia under a new provisional constitution.</p></div>
